    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Hugeicons plugin provides a seamless way to use Hugeicons in your WordPress site. This plugin is designed to make icon management and implementation as simple as possible.</p>\n<p><strong>Free Features:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Easy integration of Hugeicons into your WordPress site</li>\n<li>Icon picker interface for block editors</li>\n<li>Access to 4,300+ free icons</li>\n<li>Shortcode support</li>\n<li>Modern and responsive admin interface</li>\n<li>Compatible with latest WordPress versions</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Pro Features:</strong><br />\n<a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Upgrade to Pro</a> to unlock:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Access to 40,000+ premium icons</li>\n<li>Multiple icon styles (Solid, Duotone, Twotone, Stroke, Bulk)</li>\n<li>Multiple icon sets to choose from</li>\n<li>Regular updates with new icons</li>\n<li>Priority support</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Get Hugeicons Pro</a> to unlock all premium features!</p>\n<h3>External Services</h3>\n<p>This plugin connects to Hugeicons&#8217; servers for one essential purpose:</p>\n<p><strong>Icons API Service</strong><br />\n   * What: The plugin connects to <code>https://hugeicons.com/api</code> to fetch icon metadata and updates<br />\n   * Why: This allows us to deliver real-time icon updates, new categories, and improvements without requiring frequent plugin updates<br />\n   * When: Only when using the icon picker in the WordPress editor<br />\n   * Data transmitted: Only technical requests for icon data; no personal information is sent</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Terms of Service: <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/terms-of-service\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://hugeicons.com/terms-of-service</a></li>\n<li>Privacy Policy: <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/privacy-policy\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://hugeicons.com/privacy-policy</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Support</h3>\n<p>For support, please visit:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://hugeicons.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Hugeicons Website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://docs.hugeicons.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Documentation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://discord.gg/mauDATBZgE\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Support</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>For premium support and features, <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">upgrade to Pro</a>!</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/hugeicons</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress</li>\n<li>Use the Settings-&gt;Hugeicons screen to configure the plugin</li>\n<li>To unlock premium features, <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">upgrade to Pro</a> and enter your license key</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20add%20icons%20to%20my%20content%3F'>\nHow do I add icons to my content?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>You can add icons in several ways:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Using the Icon Picker:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Click the Hugeicons button in your editor</li>\n<li>Search and select your desired icon</li>\n<li>Insert it into your content</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Using Shortcodes:<br />\n   [hugeicons icon=&#8221;icon-name&#8221; size=&#8221;32&#8243; color=&#8221;#333333&#8243;]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Using HTML:\n   </p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</p>\n<dt id='what%27s%20the%20difference%20between%20free%20and%20pro%20versions%3F'>\nWhat&#8217;s the difference between Free and Pro versions?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Free version includes:<br />\n* 4,300+ free icons<br />\n* Standard support</p>\n<p>Pro version includes:<br />\n* 40,000+ premium icons<br />\n* Multiple icon styles<br />\n* Priority support</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Upgrade to Pro</a> to unlock all premium features!</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20upgrade%20to%20pro%3F'>\nHow do I upgrade to Pro?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<ol>\n<li>Visit <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Hugeicons Pricing</a></li>\n<li>Choose your preferred plan</li>\n<li>Complete the purchase</li>\n<li>Download the pro add-on, install it and activate it</li>\n<li>Enter your license key in the plugin settings</li>\n<li>Refresh the page and you should see the pro icons in the icon picker</li>\n</ol>\n</p>\n<dt id='what%20are%20the%20system%20requirements%3F'>\nWhat are the system requirements?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<ul>\n<li>WordPress 5.0 or higher</li>\n<li>PHP 7.4 or higher</li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>2.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Complete codebase rewrite for improved performance and maintainability</li>\n<li>Added new block widgets: FAQ, Button with Icon, Icon List, Icon Box, and Icon blocks</li>\n<li>Enhanced block editor integration with modern React components</li>\n<li>Improved icon picker interface and user experience</li>\n<li>Better code organization and architecture</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested compatibility with WordPress 6.9</li>\n<li>Updated for WordPress 6.9 release</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n<li>Added icon picker for block editor</li>\n<li>Added shortcode support</li>\n<li>Added free icon set</li>\n<li>Added Pro version support</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Add beautiful Hugeicons to your WordPress site with an easy-to-use icon picker for both classic and block editors.",
    "description": "<p>Hugeicons plugin provides a seamless way to use Hugeicons in your WordPress site. This plugin is designed to make icon management and implementation as simple as possible.</p>\n<p><strong>Free Features:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Easy integration of Hugeicons into your WordPress site</li>\n<li>Icon picker interface for block editors</li>\n<li>Access to 4,300+ free icons</li>\n<li>Shortcode support</li>\n<li>Modern and responsive admin interface</li>\n<li>Compatible with latest WordPress versions</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Pro Features:</strong><br />\n<a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Upgrade to Pro</a> to unlock:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Access to 40,000+ premium icons</li>\n<li>Multiple icon styles (Solid, Duotone, Twotone, Stroke, Bulk)</li>\n<li>Multiple icon sets to choose from</li>\n<li>Regular updates with new icons</li>\n<li>Priority support</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Get Hugeicons Pro</a> to unlock all premium features!</p>\n<h3>External Services</h3>\n<p>This plugin connects to Hugeicons&#8217; servers for one essential purpose:</p>\n<p><strong>Icons API Service</strong><br />\n   * What: The plugin connects to <code>https://hugeicons.com/api</code> to fetch icon metadata and updates<br />\n   * Why: This allows us to deliver real-time icon updates, new categories, and improvements without requiring frequent plugin updates<br />\n   * When: Only when using the icon picker in the WordPress editor<br />\n   * Data transmitted: Only technical requests for icon data; no personal information is sent</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Terms of Service: <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/terms-of-service\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://hugeicons.com/terms-of-service</a></li>\n<li>Privacy Policy: <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/privacy-policy\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://hugeicons.com/privacy-policy</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Support</h3>\n<p>For support, please visit:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://hugeicons.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Hugeicons Website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://docs.hugeicons.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Documentation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://discord.gg/mauDATBZgE\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Support</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>For premium support and features, <a href=\"https://hugeicons.com/pricing\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">upgrade to Pro</a>!</p>\n",
    "download_link": "https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/hugeicons.2.0.0.zip",
